/-!
# Tag 0A0M at an arbitrary ideal, and the properness clause, in one statement

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal, `f : X ⟶ Spec A` a Noetherian scheme over `A` and
`ℱ` a coherent `𝒪_X`-module all of whose cohomology modules `H^p(X, ℱ)` are finite over `A`.
Write `𝓘 = I · 𝒪_X`. [Stacks, Tag 0A0M] asserts that for every `p` there is a short exact sequence
of `A`-modules

`0 ⟶ R¹lim H^{p-1}(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ H^p(X, ℱ)^∧ ⟶ lim H^p(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ) ⟶ 0`,

`H^p(X, ℱ)^∧` being the `I`-adic completion of the `A`-module `H^p(X, ℱ)`, and that **if `f` is
proper the `R¹lim` term is zero**. This file proves both, for an arbitrary ideal `I`, and carries
the tag.

## What was missing, and what closes it

`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology` of
`Completion/CohomologyAdicCompletion.lean` proves the sequence from a single input `hBLX`, the
isomorphism

`C(RΓ(X, ℱ)) ≅ RΓ(X, (lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)[0])` in `D(A)`,

`C` a reflector onto the derived-complete objects of `D(A)`; and
`Stacks.Algebraization.isZero_firstDerivedLimit_cohomology_adicQuotients_of_isProper` of
`Completion/CohomologyAdicCompletionWhole.lean` proves the properness clause outright. So the
tag's one remaining input is `hBLX` at a general ideal. It is discharged here by composing three
results, each proved separately:

* the identity `RΓ(𝒞, K)^∧ = RΓ(𝒞, K^∧)` of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] at an ideal sheaf generated by
  finitely many global sections of `𝒪`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections`;
* part (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K], `ℱ^∧ = lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ` with an ordinary limit, read at `I · 𝒪_X` in
  `Stacks.Algebraization.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_limit_adicQuotients_baseIdealSheaf`;
* the comparison `RΓ(𝒞, -) ≅ RΓ(X, -)` of the ringed-site and scheme-level derived global
  sections, `Stacks.Algebraization.derivedGlobalSectionsOverSiteIso`.

`A` being Noetherian, `I = (a_1, …, a_r)`, and `I · 𝒪_X` is then the ideal sheaf generated by the
global sections `ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r` of `𝒪_X`
(`Stacks.Algebraization.baseIdealSheaf_ideal_eq_span_globalRes`), which is the regime the first
two results are proved in. Nothing is assumed: the generators are produced from the Noetherian
hypothesis, and the reflector onto the derived-complete objects of `D(A)` is produced from
[Stacks, Tag 0920] inside the proof and quantified over in the statement.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections_baseIdealSheaf`:
  `RΓ(X, ℱ)^∧ ≅ RΓ(X, lim ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)`, the identity of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] at `𝓘 = I · 𝒪_X`, with the
  derived completion taken as `DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.hBLX_baseIdealSheaf`: the same, for every reflector onto the
  derived-complete objects of `D(A)` — the shape `exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology`
  consumes.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology_of_fin_generating_family`:
  the source's short exact sequence at an ideal presented by a finite generating family.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_shortExact_adicCompletion_cohomology_whole`: **[Stacks,
  Tag 0A0M]** — the sequence at an arbitrary ideal of a Noetherian ring, together with the
  properness clause.

## Implementation notes

The properness clause is stated for every `p : ℤ`, as the sequence is. For `p - 1 ≥ 0` it is
`Stacks.Algebraization.isZero_firstDerivedLimit_cohomology_adicQuotients_of_isProper`; for
`p - 1 < 0` the tower `n ↦ H^{p-1}(X, ℱ/𝓘ⁿℱ)` is identically zero, derived global sections of a
sheaf placed in degree zero having no cohomology in negative degrees
(`Stacks.DerivedFunctor.isZero_homology_totalRightDerived_obj`), and a tower of zero objects is
Mittag-Leffler, so the `R¹lim` term vanishes there too.

`Stacks.Algebraization.modulesHasDerivedCategory` is reinstated as a local instance of high
priority, as in `Completion/CohomologyAdicCompletion.lean`, so that `D(𝒪_X)` is the standard
model, which is the one at which the ringed-site results are stated.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A06](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A06)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0920](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0920)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OB)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

